scratch_*.py
*.apk
dump.rdb

# Screenshots belong in a PR or an issue, not in the tree — CI checks out
# with --depth=1, so every one of them is downloaded on every deploy.
*_screenshot*.png
*screenshot*.png

# Written on the server by backup_db.sh and mounted into the backup bot. Real
# data, never source — but untracked and unignored it shows up in `git status`
# on the deploy host, where a dirty tree is noise nobody can act on.
backups/
.deploy-history

# Local secrets. Already covered above, kept explicit because these are the
# names that would hurt: nothing matching them has ever been committed and
# nothing should be.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Agent tooling writes these into the repo root on every run. They are runtime
# state, not source, and unignored they sit in `git status` forever — which is
# how a real change gets lost in the noise.
.swarm/
.claude-flow/
uploads/
backend/uploads/
